### GitHub Repository Integration API Tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
@githubToken = YOUR_GITHUB_TOKEN_HERE

###############################################
### SETUP: Login first to get token
###############################################

### 1. Login to get JWT token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

###############################################
### GITHUB INTEGRATION - Fetch Repositories
###############################################

### 2. Sync All Repositories from GitHub
# This fetches all repositories from your GitHub account and saves them
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 3. Sync Repositories with Explicit GitHub Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github?token={{githubToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 4. Fetch Specific Repository from GitHub
# Format: owner/repo-name
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github/repo?fullName=octocat/Hello-World
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 5. Fetch Specific Repository with GitHub Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github/repo?fullName=microsoft/vscode&token={{githubToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 6. Fetch Your Own Repository
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github/repo?fullName=YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### VERIFY SYNCED REPOSITORIES
###############################################

### 7. Get All Synced Repositories
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 8. Get Repository by ID (Use ID from sync response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories/663f7b8a9e4c1d2a3b4c5d6e
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 9. Search Synced Repositories
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories/search?query=hello
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 10. Get Repository Count
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories/count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### ERROR CASES
###############################################

### 11. Sync Without GitHub Token (Should Fail if not set in profile)
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 12. Fetch Non-Existent Repository (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github/repo?fullName=invalid/nonexistent-repo-xyz
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 13. Fetch with Invalid Format (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github/repo?fullName=invalid-format
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 14. Sync Without Authentication (Should return 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories/sync/github

###

###############################################
### UPDATE USER PROFILE WITH GITHUB TOKEN
###############################################

### 15. Update User with GitHub Token
# First, you need an endpoint to update user profile
# This is a placeholder - implement if needed
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "githubToken": "ghp_your_github_personal_access_token_here"
}

###

###############################################
### TESTING WORKFLOW
###############################################

# STEP 1: Get GitHub Personal Access Token
#   - Go to GitHub.com → Settings → Developer Settings → Personal Access Tokens
#   - Generate new token with 'repo' scope
#   - Copy the token

# STEP 2: Login and get JWT token (Test #1)
#   - Copy the accessToken

# STEP 3: Update @token and @githubToken variables at top

# STEP 4: Sync all repositories from GitHub (Test #2 or #3)
#   - This will fetch all your repositories

# STEP 5: Verify synced repositories (Tests #7-10)

# STEP 6: Fetch specific repository (Tests #4-6)

# STEP 7: Test error cases (Tests #11-14)

###

